NOT VERIFIED specular at the tick-2000 reference camera: PIN_SPEC_DIFF=0 because S1 == S2 -- only 28 px of the world are covered by the nine material-normal materials there (C vs D moves 28 px), so the lobe has no material normal to read. The consumer is measured, not assumed, at the T45 wide-area pose WALL013: S1w vs S2w = 775135 bytes, 386760 brighter / 388375 darker. That is a second view with a visible population, NOT a replacement for the missing tick-2000 one; both are pinned above.
NOT VERIFIED detail residual, pixel-level mechanism only (the cause is measured): 2812 px of the detail moved population (1320 old + 1492 new, 0.33% of the frame) sit on 27 non-displaced WOOD/WALL007A faces where the T26 face-id mask says the surface did not move and the baseline frame is byte-identical, yet the detail layer's effect toggled. T45 put T29's pre-fix near plane back (T29's own m1 patch, one expression): source 85b00d68.. -> fe39ae5d.., the product then prints 'gpu: world clip near=0.05000000 nearMapUnits=610.22 state=published', and the mutated build reproduced the pre-fix frames byte-identically (A f87f396a.., F 21cb8aa2.., 0 of 2,582,352 bytes differ); restoring the line byte-identically (cmp clean, 85b00d68..) and rebuilding reproduced this tree's frames exactly (A 6bb4d9a7.., F 2ffa7d2b..). The near clip is therefore the cause, measured at frame level and not inferred from the source diff. Evidence: evidence/t40-pixel-pins/detail-residual/ (mutation.md + readings.txt). What is NOT isolated is the pixel-level path inside the rasterizer that turns a projection change into a different detail sample on an un-clipped face; a depth-tie explanation is ruled out because a different winner would change the face id, and no shader or data defect is claimed.
NOT VERIFIED material bump direction at the tick-2000 camera: the population is one-sided there (79 brighter / 0 darker) because only 28 px of the world are covered by the nine material-normal materials, so the surviving sliver reads one way. The same reader and the same nine tiles move both ways at the T45 wide-area pose (Cw vs Dw = 688102 bytes, 203847 brighter / 484255 darker) and at tick 1200 (C12 vs R1 = 990 bytes, 458 brighter / 532 darker); both carry assert_ne positive controls.
